# bluetoothd 26B123's start-up on the USB transport, the guest's side only,
# in the `--bluetooth-trace` capture format (`hci/capture.rs`). Taken from
# the model's replay (`hci/model/tests.rs`,
# `bluetoothd_bring_up_completes_in_order`): its HCI bring-up (step table
# 0x100b38f70), the device configuration after it, the vendor commands of the
# stack's later start and the first multi-core LE scan, with the parameters
# bluetoothd sends. Addresses and names are synthetic.
#
# [1] Write BD_ADDR (sent when the platform stored an address), [4] Reset
> cmd 01 fc 06 06 05 04 03 02 42
> cmd 03 0c 00
# [5] Read Verbose Config Version Info, [6] version, [7] commands,
# [8] BD_ADDR, [9] features, [10] extended features page 2, [11] LE features
> cmd 79 fc 00
> cmd 01 10 00
> cmd 02 10 00
> cmd 09 10 00
> cmd 03 10 00
> cmd 04 10 01 02
> cmd 03 20 00
# [12] Set Event Mask, [14] LE Set Event Mask, [15] SSP mode, [16] LE host
> cmd 01 0c 08 ff ff fb ff 07 f8 bf 3d
> cmd 01 20 08 1f 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
> cmd 56 0c 01 01
> cmd 6d 0c 02 01 00
# [17] LE buffers, [19] LE states, [20] accept list, [21] buffers,
# [25] Host Buffer Size, [26] flow control, [27] erroneous data reporting
> cmd 02 20 00
> cmd 1c 20 00
> cmd 0f 20 00
> cmd 05 10 00
> cmd 33 0c 07 fd 03 00 08 00 00 00
> cmd 31 0c 01 01
> cmd 5b 0c 01 01
